TT BFP weight quantization

The B-format numerical rounding behavior is derived from Tenstorrent's tt-metal
blockfloat_common.cpp, Copyright 2026 Tenstorrent USA, Inc., licensed under
Apache License 2.0. This package provides adapted NumPy/C++ implementations with
offline exponent search, GPTQ compensation, general model APIs and calibration
helpers. It does not contain Tenstorrent model checkpoints or device kernels.

GPTQ algorithm attribution: Elias Frantar, Saleh Ashkboos, Torsten Hoefler and
Dan Alistarh, "GPTQ: Accurate Post-Training Quantization for Generative Pre-trained
Transformers", ICLR 2023, https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.17323.

The standalone Emax/Emax-1 comparison is the method proposed by Matt in the
original experiment discussion. No affiliation or endorsement is implied.
